# Measure the Sunblade's activated light field ON SCREEN, by the radius of the
# lit disc it paints around the player. Read by tools/check_sunblade_light_range.sh.
#
# bd inc-cyma (upgrade F39 / inc-tek.8.8 from Traced to Observed). The fix at
# commit e47f209 changed the Sunblade FI_LIGHT field's lval from 5 to 6
# (lib/m_items.irh). Under REPORTING-GATE that was Traced: a grep proved the
# source changed, but the game was never watched lighting a wider area.
#
# THE ORACLE is the map itself. An activated FI_LIGHT field renders as a disc of
# ',' glyphs centred on the player '@'. The disc's radius in tiles IS the field's
# lval, and one tile is ten feet. The glyph is distinct from floor '.', so the
# count is unambiguous even in an already-lit room: on seed 1 the disc stops with
# four plain floor tiles still visible before the wall, so the wall does not clip
# it. tools/oracle_ab.sh runs this file on the without-fix build (e47f209^, lval 5)
# and the with-fix build (lval 6); the check reads the '@' row of the
# after-activation dump on each and asserts 5 then 6.
#
# The wizard-mode path mirrors sunblade-cold.keys: RIGHT*10 reaches the specific
# weapons, Hornblade is the entry after Sunblade, so stopping on it leaves the
# Sunblade selected. INITIAL_PLUS 2 makes it a known +2.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10                # specific weapons
@until "Hornblade" DOWN
ENTER
2                       # Sunblade's INITIAL_PLUS
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand
SPACE
n                       # do not wield the short sword two-handed
s                       # stow the displaced starting weapon
ESC

@dump:map-before-activation

a
a                       # activate the Sunblade's 3/day light field
@dump:map-after-activation

@quit
